{"study_accession":"PRJNA679890","secondary_study_accession":"SRP294295","title":"CircRNA expression profiles in peripheral blood mononuclear cells of patients with large-artery atherosclerotic stroke","description":"Circular RNAs (circRNAs) are a recently discovered non-coding RNA isoform capable of regulating neurological disease incidence. The present study was designed to characterize the circRNA expression profiles present in large-artery atherosclerosis (LAA)-type acute ischemic stroke patients. Using a RNA-seq approach, we characterized circRNA expression profiles in 5 LAA-stroke patients and 4 controls. We identified 182 and 176 circRNAs that were up- and down-regulated, respectively, in LAA-stroke patients relative to controls. Enrichment analyses suggested these differentially expressed circRNAs to primarily be associated with chromatin modification, autophagy, platelet activation, and neural precursor cell proliferation. Overall design: Human PBMCs circRNA profiles in 5 patients with large-artery atherosclerotic stroke and 4 matched controls","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":9,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN16854251","study_accession":"PRJNA679890","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"binglizu 17","description":"binglizu 17","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM4923317","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-01-02","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["type","large-artery atherosclerotic stroke patients"],["tissue","blood"],["dev_stage","acute stage"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13093715","experiment_accession":"SRX9539314","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 3000","read_count":51217886,"base_count":15365365800,"first_public":"2022-01-02","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 3000 sequencing: GSM4923317: binglizu 17 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN16854252","study_accession":"PRJNA679890","